# Infrastructure Conventions

## Ansible

- Inventory: `ansible/inventory/hosts.ini`
- Always test with `--check` (dry run) before applying playbooks
- Roles are per-service under `ansible/roles/` (grafana, k3s_server, keycloak, matrix_synapse, etc.)
- Playbooks follow pattern: `ansible/playbooks/<service>-<action>.yml`

## Terraform

- Environment configs: `terraform/environments/homelab/`
- Reusable modules: `terraform/modules/` (k3s, keycloak, matrix, monitoring)
- Never manually edit Terraform state files
- Always `terraform plan` before `terraform apply`

## Kubernetes

- Resources organized by namespace function:
  - `communication/` -- Matrix/Synapse, Element
  - `identity/` -- Keycloak
  - `infrastructure/` -- Core infra
  - `mcp/` -- MCP server deployments
  - `monitoring/` -- Prometheus, Grafana, Loki

## Key Architectural Choices

- K3s (lightweight) over full K8s for home lab constraints
- Keycloak as central IAM for all services
- MetalLB for bare-metal load balancing
- Longhorn for distributed persistent storage
